From 87c1f4da8d8f921f696075bdc6d40fb7abd66f10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Ross <jonross@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:43:04 -0700
Subject: [Backport] CVE-2026-113012: Improper input validation in GPU

Manual cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8520423
gpu: Restore GL context/surface after WrappedSkImageBacking MakeCurrent

WrappedSkImageBacking makes its shared context current during
initialization and destruction. Restore whichever GL context was
previously current once that work is done, so callers' context state is
preserved.

Also make the passthrough decoder verify after each command that its own
context is still current. If a command left a different context current,
the decoder now marks its context as lost instead of continuing.

Bug: 568215670
Change-Id: I3fb356bbe3796c2c6c61cfc2ff2548c26f63cca4
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8520423
Commit-Queue: Jonathan Ross <jonross@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714771}
Reviewed-on: https://codereview.qt-project.org/c/qt/qtwebengine-chromium/+/783204
Reviewed-by: Moss Heim <moss.heim@qt.io>
